s892341@minyos.xx.rmit.OZ.AU (Matt=Goodall) writes:

>I had an idea similiar to this, instead of the random Dungeons of Doom you
>could have your adventurer explore somewhere else where all the levels are
>prewritten and it also has a story behind it.

>Ie the Baron wants you to clear out the giant rats from his cellar.
>There are no wandering (random) monsters and the Baron rewards you as
>you clear out various levels. Perhaps a little like Ultima.

Interesting.  There are non-D. of D. levels.  The Gnomish Mines?  The
Quest?  However, OUTDOORS adventures might be a nice thing.  Explose the
wilderness *outside* the dungeons.  Here's an idea:

Start in a town.  It's sort of like the gnomish mall, but more featureful
and full-screen; no other rooms.  A Big Room with shops, in other words. 
You start with X amount of money, a 0-level character.  Now, you buy some
basic weapons and stuff and go out and fight monsters.  You start at -10
XP, by the way.  When you hit 0 XP, you can return to the town and choose
a character class (there are guilds for each:  a School for Wizards, a
Temple for Priests, a Med School for Healers, Dr. Jones's Archaeology 101
for you-know-who, and so on.) and you gain 1st level.  The guild will give
you some weapons and armor (in addition to what little you bought or
gained by killing monsters in the outdoors)  You can return to the town
later for equipment, healing, etc. but it costs money.

BTW: The shops in the town are very burglar-proof.  Undiggable walls,
shopkeepers twice as strong, and PLENTY of watchmen with wands of death. 
Stealing from the town is a BIG no-no.

Soooo... your Guild sends you on an adventure.  You're first level, so you
get assigned to escort a caravan through dangerous terrain, and you're
more or less cannon fodder for the goblin bandits.  If you survive that,
you come back to town with maybe a 3d level guy/girl.  So you're asked to
go scout out some caves, which, incidentally, are full of buggers. 
Goblins, kobolds, and a nasty Kobold Lord and his Kobold Shaman assistants
as the bosses.

[Insert Bad Nethack Monster Joke:  What do you get if you cross a weak
Nethack monster with a net.personality?  Either a Kibold or a Gobl-_-Inston.]

So you survive enough little (and progressively bigger) quests until you
are of requisite level to enter your real quest:  to get the Amulet.  So
you go into the Dungeons of Doom and the rest is the same as normal
Nethack, except for a few things:

	* You start on what is the equivalent of about Level 10 in difficulty.
	* You can come back to the surface to buy things and get healed.
	* The Gnomish Mines and other non-D. of D. dungeons are, in fact,
other quests, and not necessarily connected to the D. of D.  The connected
ones are The Quest and the other ones you need to go through to win.

Fun?

